hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17671","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Mufaddal ibn Muhalhal narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Shibak, from al-Sha'bi, from a man from Thaqif, who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for three things and he allowed us none of them. We said: Our land is a cold land, so we asked him to allow us concession in purification, and he did not allow us. We asked him to allow us concerning Dubba' vessels, and he did not allow us in it for a time. We asked him to return Abu Bakrah to us, and he refused and said: He is the freedman of Allah and the freedman of His Messenger. Abu Bakrah had gone out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he besieged Ta'if and embraced Islam."
"17672","'Abd Allah narrated to us: al-Warkani narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas informed us, from Mughirah, from Shibak, from al-Sha'bi, from a man from Thaqif, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
